.TH detox 1 "May 2025" "detox.sh 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
detox \- scrub unwanted files from your data directory using pattern-based rules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B detox
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
detox is a lightweight CLI utility designed to recursively remove unwanted or irrelevant files from a data directory. It applies customizable pattern-based rules to ensure that only relevant and meaningful files remain.

This is particularly useful when working with scanned archives, converted text dumps, or noisy exports where useless files can clutter your workspace or pollute downstream pipelines.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -i ", " --input " <dir>"
Directory to scan and clean. Defaults to \fB./data\fR.
.TP
.BR -o ", " --output " <dir>"
Optional output directory for logs or reports. Defaults to \fB./output\fR.
.TP
.BR -d ", " --dry-run
Print the list of files that would be removed, but do not delete anything.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --verbose
Show additional details while processing.
.TP
.BR -r ", " --rules " <file>"
Path to a custom rules file. Defaults to built-in patterns if not provided.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help message and exit.

.SH CONFIGURATION
detox sources its behavior and icon styling from a configuration file (\fBdetox.conf\fR) located alongside the script. This file defines emoji/icon mappings and presentation strings used in output.

.SH USAGE EXAMPLES
.TP
.B detox
Run with default settings using \fB./data\fR as input.
.TP
.B detox -i /mnt/scrapyard -d
Preview what would be deleted from the target directory.
.TP
.B detox --rules rules/purge.txt --input archives/

